From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:39:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updater: keep the background auto-download from blocking the
 update screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Checking for updates (About screen button, app start, periodic job) also
enqueued a scheduled background download under the same unique work name as
the download started from the update screen. On 卓易通 that job can never
finish an update (no install permission, the silent PackageInstaller session
is dropped), but its ENQUEUED state made the update screen show
"downloading 0%" forever with no way to start the real download.

- Drop the background auto-download and the "auto update app" restrictions
  preference that configured it; updates are downloaded from the update
  screen only.
- Tag downloads started from the update screen and only treat those as a
  pending download while they carry no progress data yet.
- Start every download from scratch instead of resuming into a leftover
  update.apk from an earlier version, which produced a corrupt APK.
- Delete update.apk on startup once the version it holds is installed, so the
  cache directory no longer keeps the last installer around.
